You're right: giving them the failed attempts spoils the test.

I've started a third worker for the blind test, a fresh Opus. It gets only what I had when I first took up the item:
- the situation: batch 20 landed, you chose its review items, and this is the first one;
- my reasoning at that time: what landed, that the record says your answer is pending, and that the judgement says the bound "bends the letter" of P-86;
- the skill's form for an ask.

It doesn't get my failed attempts, your reactions or any instruction to write more clearly. I'll send you its draft word for word, marked "blind", next to the other two, which are marked "not blind".

